    "result_text": "AcceptanceTest is the only test class, and the full suite is green. Done.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the `contactPreference` field on the owner read model: **`EMAIL`** when the owner has an email, otherwise **`PHONE`**.\n\nChanges:\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `contactPreference` property (enum `EMAIL`/`PHONE`) to the `Owner` schema. The OpenAPI generator produces `OwnerDto.ContactPreferenceEnum` and the `contactPreference` field on `OwnerDto`.\n2. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added `@Mapping(target = \"contactPreference\", expression = \"java(toContactPreference(owner))\")` on `toOwnerDto`, plus a `toContactPreference(Owner)` helper that returns `EMAIL` when `email` is present (non-null, non-blank) and `PHONE` otherwise.\n\nThe value is derived on read (like the existing `locality`/`displayName` fields) and flows out through the existing `RespondWithOwner` OfficeFloor step on `GET /api/owners/{ownerId}`. No new endpoint wiring was needed.\n\nTests: `AcceptanceTest` (`corePhoneWhenNoEmail`, `functionalityEmailWhenPresent`) and the full suite pass \u2014 `Tests run: 2, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`, `BUILD SUCCESS`.",
